Question (issue #128): the "Run secretlint" step in quality.yml prints nothing
and finishes in ~6s on main (ci-logs/quality-37509328407.log, lines
127-135). Is it scanning anything, or is it a silent false negative?

Probe: a worktree of HEAD, with a generated GitHub token (ghp_ + 36 random
alphanumerics) and a Slack bot token written to planted-secret.txt at the root
and to js/src/x/a.txt, then the exact CI command with the versions pinned:

$ npx --yes -p secretlint@13.0.7 -p @secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend@13.0.7 \
    secretlint --secretlintignore .gitignore "**/*"
/tmp/sl-probe/repo/planted-secret.txt
  1:13  error  [GITHUB_TOKEN] found GitHub Token(...)  @secretlint/secretlint-rule-github
  2:6   error  [SLACK_TOKEN] found slack token: ...      @secretlint/secretlint-rule-slack
/tmp/sl-probe/repo/js/src/x/a.txt
  (same two findings)
✖ 4 problems (4 errors, 0 warnings, 0 infos)
exit=1

Without the planted files the same command exits 0 with no output, which is
what CI shows. Conclusion: not a false negative; silence is secretlint's
success output.

Side observations, not acted on:
- An AWS key pair whose secret contains "EXAMPLE" is not reported; AWS's own
  documentation keys use that word, so the rule treats it as a placeholder.
- A PEM block with a random base64 body between BEGIN/END RSA PRIVATE KEY
  lines was not reported either. Not investigated further.

Change made: secretlint and its preset pinned to 13.0.7 (the current latest,
`npm view secretlint version`), because `npx --yes -p secretlint` resolved the
newest release on every run.
